+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/relocating/">Relocating</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Which Town</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">13 places, from county records</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Which Grand Strand town fits you?<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">13 places near Myrtle Beach, compared.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 4, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">From Loris to Pawleys Island: where the sand is closest, where an acre is normal, where builders are selling, and what changes at the city line.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Where to live near Myrtle Beach depends on what you want most. Closest to the sand: Surfside Beach, Garden City and North Myrtle Beach. The most land: Aynor and Loris. The newest houses: Carolina Forest and Longs. The shortest drive to everything: Myrtle Beach and Socastee. The lowest prices: Conway, Loris, Longs and Socastee.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Pick the one or two things that matter most to you. The list below keeps only the places that have them.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-famil