-Surfside Beach has long called itself the family beach. It is quieter than central Myrtle Beach, with a mix of single-family homes and condominiums and steady seasonal demand, which appeals to buyers who want a calmer setting close to the action.
+## Surfside Beach, SC FAQ
 
-Common Questions
+### Is Surfside Beach part of Myrtle Beach?
+No. Surfside Beach is its own town in Horry County, incorporated in 1964, with the ZIP code 29575.
 
-## Frequently asked questions
+### Can you Airbnb in Surfside Beach?
+Only on the blocks near the ocean, in the town's R3 and C3 zoning districts. Rentals under 30 days are not allowed in the inland R1 and R2 districts.
 
-### Can you Airbnb a property in Surfside Beach?
-Only in the right zone. Surfside permits short-term rentals (under 30 days) in the R3 high-density and C3 commercial districts and restricts or prohibits them in inland R1 low-density zones. A town STR permit and safety inspection are required.
+### Can you drive a golf cart in Surfside Beach?
+Yes, on town streets posted at 35 mph or less, with a state permit decal, insurance and a licensed driver 16 or older. Never on the beach.
 
-### Is Surfside Beach a golf-cart town?
-Yes. Golf carts are a primary local mode of transport, and South Carolina allows registered carts on secondary roads during daylight within a few miles of home.
+### Are dogs allowed on Surfside Beach?
+Not from 10 a.m. to 5 p.m., May 1 through Labor Day. At other times, leashed dogs are welcome.
 
-### Why do Surfside Beach median prices look so high?
-Because the blended median mixes small inland condos with oceanfront homes. Detached single-family medians run much higher than the overall home-value index, so compare within a tier.
+### Is parking free in Surfside Beach?
+Town lots charge from March 1 to October 31, 8 a.m. to 6 p.m. An owner who lives elsewhere gets two free passes per household.
 
-### What are property taxes on a second home in Surfside Beach?
-A primary home is taxed on 4 percent of its value and does not pay the school operating tax. A second home is taxed on 6 percent and pays the school operating tax. In Surfside Beach that makes a second home's bill about 3.1 times a primary home's on the same house.
+### What is the property tax rate in Surfside Beach?
+On a home the county values at $500,000, the town and county tax is about $2,100 a year as your main home. As a second home or rental, it is about $6,400.
 
-### Which schools serve Surfside Beach?
-Public schools fall within Horry County Schools, generally Lakewood Elementary, St. James Intermediate, and St. James High. Chapter3 will confirm the exact assignment on the district boundary map.
+### What schools serve Surfside Beach?
+Horry County Schools, which assigns schools by address. We look up the assigned schools for any home you like.
 
-### Why is Surfside Beach called the family beach?
-It has a quieter, more residential feel than central Myrtle Beach, with steady seasonal demand and a mix of homes and condominiums.
+### What about crime in Surfside Beach?
+We do not rate places for crime. The town has its own police department, and the FBI publishes the crime each police agency reports.
