-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span><span><strong>Channel houses</strong><span class="t">About 680</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8.5 18.5V3.5l8 3.6-8 3.6M3.5 19c0-1.4 3.8-2.5 8.5-2.5s8.5 1.1 8.5 2.5-3.8 2.5-8.5 2.5-8.5-1.1-8.5-2.5z"/><circle cx="16" cy="15.2" r="1.2"/></svg></span><span><strong>Barefoot golf</strong><span class="t">4 courses</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>Nightly rentals</strong><span class="t">City license</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 4, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Its own city at the north end of the Grand Strand, made from four beach towns in 1968, with its own rental rules and city tax.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Myrtle Beach has about nine miles of beach and eight parts, each suited to a different buyer. For a boat behind the house, look in Cherry Grove. For Main Street and a maritime forest, look in Ocean Drive. For a house near the ocean for less, look in Crescent Beach or Windy Hill. For newer houses and little flood zone, look across the waterway or west of US 17.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A typical resold house sold for about $565,000 in the past year, from about $410,000 in Crescent Beach to $725,000 in Tilghman Beach. Nightly rentals need a yearly city business license, with no special rental zoning or permit.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Tell us how you will use the home. We will send the parts and houses that fit.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Send me North Myrtle Beach homes</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#parts" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The eight parts</a></li><li><a href="#living-here" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Living here</a></li><li><a href="#prices" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Prices</a></li><li><a href="#flood" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Flood zone</a></li><li><a href="#yearly-cost" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Yearly cost</a></li><li><a href="#renting" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Renting it out</a></li><li><a href="#pros-and-cons" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Pros and cons</a></li><li><a href="#north-myrtle-beach-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">North Myrtle Beach FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="parts"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The eight parts">Which part of North Myrtle Beach should you look in?</h2><style>
