+</style><style>main#main .hx-strip:empty{display:none}main#main .hx-strip:not(:empty)+.hx-fallback{display:none}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town calls itself the Family Beach. Its center is the pier, at the ocean end of Surfside Drive.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The pier</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town's fishing pier is all concrete and reaches 814 feet into the ocean. It opened on the town's 60th birthday, and walking on it is free.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-pier-from-above-2026-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-pier-from-above-2026-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-surfside-beach/surfside-beach-pier-from-above-2026-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Aerial photo of the Surfside Beach Pier, labelled, running from a wide beach into a green ocean, with parking lots and rows of beach houses behind the sand" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>The concrete pier from the air, with the beach parking lots and the streets of beach houses behind it.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The pier has two restaurants, The Whistling Duck and Surf Diner, plus an ice cream shop and a bait shop. A day of fishing is $14. From April through October it stays open until 1 a.m.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">A year of town events</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town has its own events department, and many of its events are free. Many take place at the pier, on Ocean Boulevard or in Memorial Park.</p><ul class="c3-sb-rules"><li><strong>Spring</strong>A two-day barbecue festival with a cook-off in March. A kite festival at the pier in April. The Memorial Day golf cart parade down Ocean Boulevard.</li><li><strong>Summer</strong>A free concert in Memorial Park, next to the library, on Sundays from 4 to 7 p.m. The Fourth of July golf cart parade, free to join.</li><li><strong>Fall</strong>An end-of-summer fireworks festival at the pier in September, with free shuttles from the town's parking lots.</li><li><strong>All season</strong>An arts and crafts market every Thursday from March to November, at Surfside Drive and Willow Drive. The Yuletide golf cart parade in December.</li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Golf carts</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most trips here need a car or a golf cart. To drive a cart on the street, South Carolina law requires a DMV permit decal, liability insurance and a licensed driver 16 or older.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Carts may use only roads posted at 35 mph or less, and never the sand. A cart driven at night must have working headlights and taillights. The town passed its own golf cart ordinance in 2025.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The beach</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town has 36 public beach accesses and 12 beach parking lots. Five accesses have wheelchair access, and beach wheelchairs are available through the town police department.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/surfside-beach-houses-from-the-sand-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/surfside-beach-houses-from-the-sand-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/surfside-beach-houses-from-the-sand-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 720px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A row of two- and three-story beach houses in blue, yellow and gray behind low dunes, seen across a wide sand beach under a blue sky at Surfside Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: BullDawg2021. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: BullDawg2021</a></span></div><figcaption>Beach houses along the sand at Surfside Beach.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">An owner who lives elsewhere gets two free parking passes per household for the town's lots. The town's lots charge by the hour from March through October. Dogs stay off the beach from 10 a.m. to 5 p.m., May through Labor Day.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Surfside%20Beach">Get the homes for sale in Surfside Beach<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far is everything?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Drive times by car from the pier, without traffic. Summer traffic on US 17 Business is slower.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">From the Surfside Beach Pier to</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">By car, about</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Food Lion on US 17 Business</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">5 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Garden City Pier</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">6 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach State Park</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">11 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Tidelands Waccamaw Community Hospital</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">12 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The MarshWalk in Murrells Inlet</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">12 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Market Common</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">14 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach International Airport</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">15 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Broadway at the Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">20 min</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="own-town"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Its own town">Is Surfside Beach part of Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Surfside Beach is its own town in Horry County, incorporated in 1964, with its own council, police department and beach rules. Its mailing ZIP code is 29575.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A "Surfside Beach" address does not prove a home is in the town. Of the homes for sale with that address when we counted, about two in three were outside the town limits.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Those homes are on county land, where the town's rental rules do not apply. Horry County's zoning has no limit on how long a home there may be rented, but a subdivision's recorded rules can. We read those rules for the home you like.</p><div class="c3-sb-note"><b>How the town began.</b> Much of its land was once the Ark Plantation. The beach was later called Roach's Beach, then Floral Beach, and took the name Surfside Beach in 1952. Hurricane Hazel in 1954 destroyed 18 of the 65 houses then at the beach.</div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What do you own at Ocean Lakes?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Ocean Lakes Family Campground is next to the town's north end, about 7 minutes from the pier by car, and it is not in the town. It has about 2,600 sites leased by the year.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At Ocean Lakes you buy the house, mobile home or camper on the site, not the land. The site comes with a yearly lease from the campground, and we go through it with you before you offer.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Ocean%20Lakes">Ask about a home in Ocean Lakes<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="rental-map"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Rental map">Where can you rent by the night in Surfside Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Nightly rentals are allowed only on the blocks near the ocean, the orange band on the map. The town calls them its R3 and C3 zones, and its own zoning sheet names R3 "High Density/Weekly Rental".</p><figure class="c3-sb-fig"><svg class="c3-sb-defs" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="0" height="0" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" style="position:absolute;width:0;height:0;overflow:hidden"><defs><g id="c3-sb-mapg"><rect x="0" y="0" width="5227" height="1851" fill="#f1ece3"/><rect x="0" y="1851" width="5227" height="520" fill="#cfe2e8"/><path d="M5224 946L5221 972L5226 977L5219 1052L5191 1128L5182 1165L5180 1262L5173 1306L5152 1368L5054 1348L4958 1822L3932 1838L4189 828L4499 868L5199 943L5224 946Z" fill="#e6e0d5" stroke="#8a8378" stroke-width="10" stroke-dasharray="40 26"/><path d=