 Military Appreciation Days National Flood Insurance Program Parking Meters Resident Parking Decals SC's Largest Garage Sale Special Events Starting or Relocating a Business Tents, Umbrellas & Shading Devices Victim Advocate Office Wall of Service Pay Parking Meter Ticket Traffic/Criminal Ticket Utility Bill Report Code Violations Request for Rezoning Service Requests Watch City Council Online Careers Apply Online (Jobs) Employee Benefits Human Resources Employee Portal Services Bicycle Map & Routes Bids & Procurement Chair/Umbrella Rentals & Accessibility Code Enforcement & Quality of Life Court Flood Protection Friday Fax Memo Hurricane Preparedness Opioid Response Program Parking Meters Pay My Bill Pay My Bill Police-to-Citizen (P2C) Reports Receive Emergency Alerts Resident Parking Decal Program Special Events Service Requests Solid Waste & Recycling Special Events Surplus Auction Items Utility Billing & Service Departments Business License Division Capital Projects Department City Attorney's Office City Manager's Office City of Myrtle Beach Municipal Court Construction Services Department Community Engagement Office Communications and Creative Services Department Economic Development Office Emergency Management Division Financial Management & Reporting Financial Services Department Fire Department GIS Division Human Resources Department Insurance & Risk Services Myrtle Beach Convention Center Neighborhood Services Department Opioid Response Program Parks, Recreation & Sports Tourism Department Planning & Zoning Department Police Department Public Works Department Procurement Division Solid Waste & Recycling Division Sports Tourism Division Utility Billing Division Victim Advocate Division Government Boards, Commissions & Committees City Attorney's Office City Manager's Office Form of Government Friday Fax Memo Mayor & City Council Meeting Schedule & Agendas Polling Places & Elections Visitors About Myrtle Beach Beach Conditions & Laws Beach Water Quality Bicycle Maps & Routes City Events List Conventions Golf Cart Laws Host a Special Event Rent a Facility SC's Largest Garage Sale Tents & Umbrellas Military Appreciation Days Vacation Information Go Home   I Want To   Apply For  Resident Parking Decal Helpful Links Parking Meters Resident Parking Decal Program To learn more about city meters, visit our Parking Meters web page. Reimagined Parking Office (Pavilion Parking Garage) 914 North Kings Highway 9:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m., Mondays-Fridays OVERVIEW The City of Myrtle Beach’s residential parking decals are available to city residents who have personal vehicles or motorcycles that "live" in the city limits and on which city property taxes have been paid.  The city counts property taxes paid on vehicles as a parking payment, whether or not the owner uses public parking.  Everyone pays for parking, just in different ways.  Residents can submit requests online or in-person Monday through Friday, 9:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m., at the Lanier Parking Office. Reimagined Parking Office Pavilion Parking Garage, 9 14 North Kings Highway (Ninth Avenue North Entrance) Myrtle Beach, South Carolina 29577 2025-26 DECALS & REQUIRED MATERIALS What you'll need...   Residents need the up-to-date South Carolina vehicle registration card, driver's license and current Horry County vehicle property tax receipt for each vehicle to receive a decal.  If residents own a qualifying golf cart, also include the South Carolina Golf Cart permit number issued by the South Carolina Department of Motor Vehicles.  Your South Carolina Driver's License address must match your Horry County Vehicle Paid Tax Receipt.  (If you do not have your vehicle tax receipt, you can look it up through  Horry County's Tax Payments & Receipts  portal.)   Customers can submit requests online or in-person at the Lanier Parking Office in the Pavilion Parking Garage, 914 North Kings Highway (Ninth Avenue North Entrance), 9:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday.  (NOTE:  Residents who have not had a parking decal in the past will need to apply in-person.)  To receive decals in-person, bring the materials listed above to the Pavilion Parking Garage.  For online registration, see below.   Each decal is specific to each vehicle; decals are not interchangeable or transferrable.  Replacement decals due to windshield damage, transfer of ownership, loss of decal or other cause are available for $20 each, upon presentation of valid property tax and registration information.  When selling or trading your vehicle, if you remove the parking decal from the old vehicle and present it when applying for a new decal, you can avoid the $20 replacement charge.   COMMERCIAL USE VEHICLES Commercial use vehicles are not eligible for the Resident Parking Decal.  However, the owner of an in-city business who also lives inside the city and uses a company-registered vehicle as his/her sole personal vehicle may qualify for a decal for that vehicle.    To download the Business Vehicle Parking Decal Affirmation Application, click here . IN-PERSON DECAL REGISTRATION Residents can submit requests online or in-person at the Reimagined Parking Office in the Pavilion Parking Garage, 914 North Kings Highway (Ninth Avenue North Entrance), 9:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m., Monday through Friday.  Customers who have not had a parking decal in the past will need to apply in-person. What you'll need...  Residents need the up-to-date South Carolina vehicle registration card, driver's license and current Horry County vehicle property tax receipt for each vehicle to receive a decal.  If residents own a qualifying golf cart, also include the South Carolina Golf Cart permit number issued by the South Carolina Department of Motor Vehicles.  Your South Carolina Driver's License address must match your Horry County Vehicle Paid Tax Receipt.  ( If you do not have your vehicle tax receipt, you can look it up through Horry County's Tax Payments & Receipts portal .)  NOTE:  If you have not paid the City of Myrtle Beach vehicle property tax, you cannot receive a Resident Parking Decal for your personal vehicle.  However, non-resident parking decals are available for $100 per year for defined areas.  See our Parking Meters webpage for more information about these and other parking details. ONLINE DECAL REGISTRATION The online parking decal registration process below is for residents who have had a parking decal issued in the past.  Each decal is specific to each vehicle; decals are not interchangeable or transferrable.  After processing, parking decals are mailed to the registered address.  What you'll need...  Residents need the up-to-date South Carolina vehicle registration card, driver's license and current Horry County vehicle property tax receipt for each vehicle to receive a decal.  If residents own a qualifying golf cart, also include the South Carolina Golf Cart permit number issued by the South Carolina Department of Motor Vehicles.  Your South Carolina Driver's License address must match your Horry County Vehicle Paid Tax Receipt.  (If you do not have your vehicle tax receipt, you can look it up through Horry County's Tax Payments & Receipts portal.)   At the moment, vehicle property tax data in this system is current from November 1, 2023 through September 30, 2026 , but will be updated monthly. If you paid your taxes after September 30, you may take your tax receipt and vehicle registration to the Myrtle Beach Parking Office in the Pavilion Parking Garage, corner of Kings Highway and Ninth Avenue (entrance on Ninth Avenue North) to receive a parking decal, or wait until the most recent monthly data is posted here. If you do not have your vehicle tax receipt, you can look it up on Horry County’s Tax Payments and Receipts website . PLEASE HAVE ALL MATERIALS READY AND FOLLOW ALL INSTRUCTIONS.  ALSO, ENTER YOUR NAME EXACTLY AS IT APPEARS ON THE VEHICLE TAX RECEIPT.   CLICK HERE TO BEGIN THE REGISTRATION PROCESS.   If any of the following apply, you WILL NOT be able to use the online registration system.  Instead, please apply for your decal in-person at the Reef Parking Office, 914 North Kings Highway, Monday through Friday, 9:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. I have not received a decal in the past. I no longer have the vehicle listed on my Horry County Vehicle Paid Tax Receipt. I am a new resident of the City of Myrtle Beach and did not pay city vehicle property tax in the current calendar year. I moved into the City of Myrtle Beach after I paid my Horry County Vehicle Property Tax. City of Myrtle Beach P.O. Box 2468 Myrtle Beach, SC 29578 info@cityofmyrtlebeach.com Powered By Revize Login × Share this page Copy and past this code into your website. <a href="http://cms5.revize.com/revize/troymi/">Your Link Name</a> Share this page on your favorite Social network Facebook Twitter Google Plus Reddit Close 
