-  title: 'Which Grand Strand Town Fits You? Prices and Rules Compared',
-  description: 'Conway to Pawleys Island, what differs between Grand Strand towns: price ranges, city versus county rules, what each area is known for, and drive times.',
-  headline: 'Which Grand Strand Town Fits You? Prices and Rules Compared',
-  keywords: 'best area to live Myrtle Beach, Grand Strand towns compared, where to live Myrtle Beach SC',
-  breadcrumb: [{ name: 'Buyers', href: '/buyers/' }, { name: 'Relocating', href: '/buyers/relocating/' }, { name: 'Which Town', href: '/buyers/relocating/which-town/' }],
-  faq,
-  main: ({ faqHtml, bylineDate }) => `
-<div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/relocating/">Relocating</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Which Town</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Town by town</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Which Grand Strand town fits you?<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">Prices and rules, compared.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated ${bylineDate}</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Prices town by town from Conway to Pawleys Island, what changes inside city limits, traffic in season and off, and where the Chapter3 team chose to live.</p><div style="margin-top:1.8rem;display:flex;gap:.75rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="#lead-form">Shortlist my towns</a><a class="btn btn-outline btn-lg" href="tel:+18543332135">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div></div>
-
-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">The short answer</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">Four things to compare before you pick a town</h2><p style="${S.p}">People search Myrtle Beach and then buy somewhere else on this list, because the name covers about sixty miles of coast plus the inland towns behind it. Compare these four differences first.</p><div class="wt-grid"><div class="wt-cell"><span class="wt-n">1</span><span class="wt-t">City limits, or unincorporated county</span><span class="wt-d">Incorporated towns set their own sales tax, trash pickup, parking decals, zoning, golf cart and rental rules. Unincorporated areas follow county rules for all of it.</span></div><div class="wt-cell"><span class="wt-n">2</span><span class="wt-t">What your budget reaches</span><span class="wt-d">The starting price in Conway and the starting price on Pawleys Island are more than $300,000 apart for similar houses.</span></div><div class="wt-cell"><span class="wt-n">3</span><span class="wt-t">Has special features you like</span><span class="wt-d">Marinas. Golf. A fishing pier. Acreage. Marsh views. New construction. Historic streets. Beach houses. The table below has each area&#39;s.</span></div><div class="wt-cell"><span class="wt-n">4</span><span class="wt-t">The drive</span><span class="wt-d">Is the location close enough to everything you need? Work, the airport, the stores you go to weekly. Measure it before you offer.</span></div></div><style>.wt-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(340px,1fr));gap:1px;background:var(--rule);border:1px solid var(--rule);max-width:900px;margin-top:.4rem}.wt-cell{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.35rem;background:var(--ivory);padding:1.15rem 1.2rem}.wt-n{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--brass);line-height:1}.wt-t{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.95rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.35}.wt-d{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.84rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.55}</style></div></section>
-
-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">Side by side</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">The towns, with prices and rules</h2>
-<div style="overflow-x:auto;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.9rem;color:var(--navy);min-width:680px"><thead><tr><th style="${S.th}">Area</th><th style="${S.th}">Price range</th><th style="${S.th}">Governed by</th><th style="${S.th}">What it is known for</th></tr></thead><tbody>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/little-river/', 'Little River')}</td><td style="${S.td}">$150,000 to $800,000</td><td style="${S.td}">Unincorporated county</td><td style="${S.td}">Intracoastal Waterway marinas and fishing docks</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">Longs, inland</td><td style="${S.td}">Typically below the beach towns</td><td style="${S.td}">Unincorporated county</td><td style="${S.td}">Acreage, affordable and rural</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/north-myrtle-beach/', 'North Myrtle Beach')}</td><td style="${S.td}">$300,000 to $2,500,000+</td><td style="${S.td}">City</td><td style="${S.td}">Wide beaches, beach houses and Ocean Drive</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/myrtle-beach/', 'Myrtle Beach')}</td><td style="${S.td}">$150,000 to $1,500,000+</td><td style="${S.td}">City</td><td style="${S.td}">The boardwalk, the most shops and restaurants</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/carolina-forest/', 'Carolina Forest')}</td><td style="${S.td}">Mostly newer construction</td><td style="${S.td}">Unincorporated county</td><td style="${S.td}">The newest construction, master-planned</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/conway/', 'Conway')}</td><td style="${S.td}">$120,000 to $500,000</td><td style="${S.td}">City</td><td style="${S.td}">A historic downtown on the Waccamaw River</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/surfside-beach/', 'Surfside Beach')}</td><td style="${S.td}">$250,000 to $1,500,000</td><td style="${S.td}">Town</td><td style="${S.td}">A fishing pier and a small-town beach grid</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/garden-city/', 'Garden City')}</td><td style="${S.td}">$225,000 to $1,200,000</td><td style="${S.td}">Mostly unincorporated county</td><td style="${S.td}">A peninsula between the ocean and the salt marsh</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/murrells-inlet/', 'Murrells Inlet')}</td><td style="${S.td}">$200,000 to $1,000,000+</td><td style="${S.td}">Unincorporated county</td><td style="${S.td}">The MarshWalk restaurants on the saltwater creek</td></tr>
-<tr><td style="${S.td}">${A('/submarkets/pawleys-island/', 'Pawleys Island')}</td><td style="${S.td}">$450,000 to $5,000,000+</td><td style="${S.td}">Town, plus unincorporated mainland</td><td style="${S.td}">Historic beach cottages, expensive, creek on one side, ocean on the other</td></tr>
-</tbody></table></div>
-<p style="${S.small};margin-top:.9rem">Price ranges are the working ranges on each area page and move with the market. Longs has no area page yet; prices there vary widely with land. Our page on the ${A('/buyers/affordable-places-to-live/', 'most affordable places to buy a home near Myrtle Beach')} compares Longs with Loris, Aynor, Conway and Georgetown. If you plan to rent the home out, the town ordinance and the HOA covenants for the address govern, and we will pull both. The feature column is what each area is physically known for, not a judgement about it. The town of Pawleys Island is entirely in Georgetown County. A Murrells Inlet mailing address can be in Horry County or in Georgetown County, which changes which county rules apply. The rules on the sand itself, dogs, tents and parking, differ by town as well, on our ${A('/buyers/relocating/beaches/', 'beach rules page')}. For the hospital nearest any address, see the ${A('/buyers/relocating/healthcare/', 'healthcare page')}.</p>
-<div style="${S.ctaBox}"><p style="margin:0;color:var(--navy);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;font-weight:600">Not sure which of these your budget reaches?</p><div style="display:flex;gap:.7rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-brass" href="#lead-form">Shortlist my towns</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="tel:+18543332135">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div></div></section>
-
-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">City or county</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">Incorporated or unincorporated: what changes</h2><p style="${S.p}">Incorporated means the address sits inside a city or town that runs its own services and writes its own rules. Unincorporated means the county does both. It does not show up in a listing, and it changes four bills.</p><h3 style="${S.h3}">Sales tax</h3><p style="${S.p}">Nine percent inside the City of Myrtle Beach, eight percent in the county. Groceries are untaxed either way.</p><h3 style="${S.h3}">Trash</h3><p style="${S.p}">Curbside collection is a city service. Outside city limits you arrange it yourself, and the options and costs are on the ${A('/buyers/relocating/moving-checklist/', 'new resident checklist')}.</p><h3 style="${S.h3}">Beach parking</h3><p style="${S.p}">The free resident parking decal is issued by the city to city residents. Living two streets outside the line means paying at the meters.</p><h3 style="${S.h3}">The HOA is separate from all of it</h3><p style="${S.p}">City limits decide the four bills above. The covenants on your deed decide how you live in the house, and they apply whether you are inside a town or not. Most newer neighborhoods here have an association; older streets and rural land often do not. Before you offer, read what the covenants say about boats, campers, work vehicles, fences, sheds, pools, exterior paint and pets, and read what the dues cover. We pull the ${A('/hoa/documents/', 'documents')} for any address, and the ${A('/hoa/', 'HOA guides')} explain ${A('/hoa/dues-increases/', 'dues increases')}, ${A('/hoa/special-assessments/', 'special assessments')} and ${A('/hoa/violations-and-fines/', 'violations and fines')} before you are living with them.</p><h3 style="${S.h3}">Golf carts and rentals</h3><p style="${S.pLast}">Each town writes its own golf cart rules, and the county writes them for unincorporated areas, so a cart that is street-legal in one neighborhood may not be in the next. Renting your house out works the same way: the town or county decides, and your HOA can say no on top of that. Check the rules for the specific address, not the town name.</p></div></section>
-
-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">The drive</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">Traffic analysis, on season and off</h2><p style="${S.p}">Traffic in our area is light, and it does not change much in peak season. Every row below is the same ten mile drive, so the areas compare directly.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.9rem;color:var(--navy);min-width:460px"><thead><tr><th style="${S.th}">A 10 mile drive from</th><th style="${S.th}">Off season</th><th style="${S.th}">On season</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="${S.td}">Surfside Beach</td><td style="${S.td}">about 19 min</td><td style="${S.td}">about 24 min</td></tr><tr><td style="${S.td}">Carolina Forest</td><td style="${S.td}">about 20 min</td><td style="${S.td}">about 25 min</td></tr><tr><td style="${S.td}">Conway</td><td style="${S.td}">about 18 min</td><td style="${S.td}">about 23 min</td></tr><tr><td style="${S.td}">Murrells Inlet</td><td style="${S.td}">about 15 min</td><td style="${S.td}">about 20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="${S.td}">North Myrtle Beach</td><td style="${S.td}">about 15 min</td><td style="${S.td}">about 20 min</td></tr><tr><td style="${S.td}">Pawleys Island</td><td style="${S.td}">about 13 min</td><td style="${S.td}">about 18 min</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="${S.p};margin-top:1.1rem">The differences come from the roads, not the distance. Ten miles on US-17 through the beach towns runs slower because of the traffic lights. Ten miles on SC-31 or SC-22 runs quicker because there are almost none, and that is the route locals take all summer.</p><p style="${S.p}">On season adds about five minutes to a ten mile drive. That is what our team plans on from driving these roads, not a measurement. Summer weekends on US-17 are the exception and run longer than that.</p><p style="${S.pLast}">If you will be working here, measure your own commute before you offer. The freeways, the two US 17s and the airport are on our ${A('/buyers/relocating/getting-around/', 'getting around page')}, and the ${A('/buyers/relocating/jobs/', 'jobs page')} covers what work here pays.</p></div></section>
-
-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">Where we landed</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">The people who wrote this page chose their own towns this way</h2><p style="${S.p}">One of our team lives in Murrells Inlet. The office is close, the stores and restaurants he likes are close, the beach is close, and Market Common with its bookstore is a short drive. He leaves the area only for training at Fitness Edge MMA in Carolina Forest. Abdulla, who builds our tools, made the same choice and lives in Murrells Inlet too. His gym is Crunch by the mall, further toward Myrtle Beach, and everything else on his list was already nearby.</p><p style="${S.p}">Two client moves show how different the right answer gets. A North Carolina family who wanted land and a house built to their own plan bought in Longs, which is inland, rural and affordable enough that the dream house fit the budget, and they commute. A New York couple went the other direction entirely: a beachfront home in North Myrtle Beach with ocean views, close to places to go out, and near the waterway because they own a boat and wanted to finally use it. Same coast, opposite answers, both correct.</p><p style="${S.pLast}">Two misconceptions we correct weekly. First, that Myrtle Beach is one big party strip. The entertainment district is there, and it is compact; leave the downtown blocks and you are in quiet residential streets, some of them expensive, and within a short drive of the entertainment district. Second, that the whole area is a retirement community. About 30 percent of the county is 65 or older, which means about 70 percent is not, and there is a university campus in Conway. Every age buys here, and we work with all of them.</p></div></section>
-
-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><p style="${S.eyebrow}">How we do this</p><h2 style="${S.h2}">We give you the records, not our opinion of a neighborhood</h2><p style="${S.p}">Fair housing law is strict about agents steering buyers toward or away from areas, and it is strict for good reason. That is why we do not describe who lives in an area, and you should be wary of any agent who does.</p><p style="${S.p}">Instead we hand over what is written down. Zoning and short-term rental rules are municipal ordinances. Rental caps and minimum lease terms are in the HOA covenants. Flood zones are on the federal maps. School attendance zones are on the state and district lookup tools, which the ${A('/buyers/relocating/schools/', 'schools page')} shows you how to use. Every one of those is a document you can read yourself, and we will get you all of them for any address before you make an offer.</p><p style="${S.pLast}">Tell us what the house has to do and what it has to be near. That is a question about property, and it is one we can answer properly.</p></div></section>
-
